  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Folk-song and dance repertoire of Turkey's eastern Black Sea provinces — Trabzon, Rize, Artvin, Giresun — collected from the 1930s by Ankara Radio ekipleri and popularized nationally from the 1970s by Volkan Konak, Kâzım Koyuncu and Birol Topaloğlu, built on the three-string kemençe's fast bowed double-stops and the tulum bagpipe's drone over rapid 7/16 and 2/4 horon rhythms, with tight nasal shouted vocals and short repeated melodic cells.",
